{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model using weighted fusion (vs. concat in config_018) with RNA (pca_n2000) and image (resnet50) data, achieving validation accuracy of 0.639 (F1: 0.620). The result suggests weighted fusion may offer marginal improvement over concat, though performance remains lower than the RNA-only multiprofile baseline (0.650). Uncertainty persists about the relative effectiveness of fusion strategies and the contribution of image data, as no other fusion methods or encoder combinations have been evaluated."
}

